    <description>ALF-RS-10 (LFRDN-340) FR1/AC1: Quick Action screen flow wrapping AF_SalesOrderService.generate() so the rep gets a visible result - the service itself only returns a Result object with no UI, so calling it as a bare Apex quick action would show nothing on success and a generic failure toast on a gate block instead of the specific DEC-014 message. Mirrors AF_FL_Reservation_GenerateContract (ALF-RS-08/LFRDN-338 FR14). 2026-09-19: start goes straight to Screen_ConfirmPayment, skipping the former opening Required Documents screen (still present as Screen_RequiredDocuments, just unreachable) - that screen hosted afDocumentComponent pointed at AF_DynamicObject__mdt.SalesOrder / AF_DocumentCondition__mdt.SalesOrder_All, but no AF_Document__mdt rows exist for Sales Order (BRD names no specific documents), so it rendered as a confusing always-empty checklist with no gating effect (Next always worked regardless). Re-wire the start connector back to Screen_RequiredDocuments if the business later defines real Sales Order document requirements. LFRDN-662 FR4: added Screen_ConfirmPayment before Call_Sales_Order_Service - the rep must actively confirm payment has been collected (shown the actual paid/outstanding amounts) before the Sales Order is generated; declining exits cleanly via Screen_Cancelled with nothing created. The confirming user is stamped onto Opportunity.AF_SOPaymentConfirmedBy__c by AF_SalesOrderService in the same transaction as generation. The underlying data-layer gate (AF_VR_Opp_SOGenerationGate / AF_SalesOrderService.findBlocker()) remains the authoritative check, since this prompt only covers the UI path - the API path has no prompt and relies on that gate alone.</description>
